<p>Err, to be honest, I didn't particularly like it. Very hesitant neutral vote, though; good presentation and execution in the later half of the second log saved it. The &quot;oh crap, they were warning us&quot; bit was nice, I'll admit.</p>
<p>This article is conceptually just another reiteration of the &quot;tale presented in the form of an expedition log&quot; quasi-format-screw trope. It doesn't have a particularly throat-grabbing idea to begin with; it just feels like a generic thing what kills you. If you'd written in typical fashion with a more detailed description and a less prominent log, it wouldn't be particularly fascinating. And the first log is way too informal. It largely would have been redacted.</p>
<p>Unless I'm missing something, this is a weak article.</p>
