														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2714333">
									

<p>It's&#8230;not a format screw? Criticizing an article for having the narrative mainly in the form of exploration logs is like criticizing a novel for having a story told mainly through flashbacks - it's a storytelling device. It's one way in which you can convey information. Many of djkaktus' works, for example, rely on this way of moving the plot forward.</p>
<p>There are also several SCPs for which the point is not the effect in itself - they act more as a vehicle for the narrative. This is one of those where it doesn't revolve centrally around the nature of the SCP itself - it is more about the discovery and escape from it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
